═══ PER-COMMAND --help ═══

────────── botmap download --help ──────────
Usage: botmap download [OPTIONS]

Options:
  --bbox BBOX
  --in TEXT                       Resolve a place name to a bbox via the
                                  divisions index.
  --where TEXT                    Attribute filter K OP V (repeatable).
                                  Example: --where height>50
  -f [geojson|geojsonseq|geoparquet]
                                  [required]
  -o, --output PATH
  -t, --type [address|bathymetry|building|building_part|division|division_area|division_boundary|place|segment|connector|infrastructure|land|land_cover|land_use|water]
                                  [required]
  -r, --release TEXT              Release version (defaults to latest)
  --stac / --no-stac              By default, uses the STAC catalog to limit
                                  which Parquet files are downloaded. Pass
                                  --no-stac to skip the catalog and read the
                                  full S3 dataset directly.
  --connect_timeout INTEGER
  --request_timeout INTEGER
  --help                          Show this message and exit.

────────── botmap gers --help ──────────
Usage: botmap gers [OPTIONS] GERS_ID

  Query the GERS registry for a feature by its GERS ID.

  By default, this command only queries the registry and displays information
  about the feature (version, filepath, bbox, etc.) without downloading the
  feature data.

  To download the actual feature data, specify an output format using
  -f/--format.

Options:
  -f [geojson|geojsonseq|geoparquet]
                                  Output format. If not specified, only
                                  registry information will be displayed.
  -o, --output PATH
  --connect_timeout INTEGER
  --request_timeout INTEGER
  --help                          Show this message and exit.

────────── botmap where --help ──────────
Usage: botmap where [OPTIONS] QUERY

  Resolve a place name to an Overture division feature.

Options:
  --all                  Show all matching divisions, not just the best one.
  --geometry, --geojson  Emit the division's polygon as a GeoJSON Feature on
                         stdout (for clipping/spatial joins). Replaces
                         `download -t division_area`.
  --help                 Show this message and exit.

────────── botmap boundary --help ──────────
Usage: botmap boundary [OPTIONS] QUERY

  Emit a division's polygon as a GeoJSON Feature (for clipping/spatial joins).

  QUERY is a place name, e.g. 'Alameda County, CA' or 'Brooklyn, NY'. Outputs
  the division_area polygon on stdout — pipe to files or spatial tools.

Options:
  --help  Show this message and exit.

────────── botmap count --help ──────────
Usage: botmap count [OPTIONS]

  Count features for a query without downloading them.

Options:
  -t, --type [address|bathymetry|building|building_part|division|division_area|division_boundary|place|segment|connector|infrastructure|land|land_cover|land_use|water]
                                  [required]
  --bbox BBOX
  --in TEXT
  --where TEXT
  -r, --release TEXT
  --help                          Show this message and exit.

