────────── botmap schema --help ──────────
Usage: botmap schema [OPTIONS]

  Show the schema and a sample feature for an Overture type.

  Uses a tiny bbox over a known-populated area to keep this fast.

Options:
  -t, --type [address|bathymetry|building|building_part|division|division_area|division_boundary|place|segment|connector|infrastructure|land|land_cover|land_use|water]
                                  [required]
  -r, --release TEXT
  --help                          Show this message and exit.

────────── botmap categories --help ──────────
Usage: botmap categories [OPTIONS]

  Enumerate `categories.primary` values, sorted by count desc.

Options:
  -t, --type TEXT     Feature type to enumerate. Only `place` is supported;
                      other types use `class` — see `botmap schema -t TYPE`.
                      [default: place]
  --bbox BBOX
  --in TEXT
  --top INTEGER       [default: 20]
  -r, --release TEXT
  --help              Show this message and exit.

────────── botmap capabilities --help ──────────
Usage: botmap capabilities [OPTIONS]

  Emit a machine-readable manifest of all subcommands.

Options:
  --help  Show this message and exit.

────────── botmap places --help ──────────
Usage: botmap places [OPTIONS]

  Download POIs in a named place. Filter by --category for common asks.

Options:
  --in TEXT                       Resolve a place name to a bbox via the
                                  divisions index.
  --bbox BBOX                     Bounding box xmin,ymin,xmax,ymax. Mutually
                                  exclusive with --in.
  --category TEXT                 Shortcut for --where categories.primary=VAL
  --where TEXT
  -n, --limit INTEGER             Maximum number of features to emit (default:
                                  all matches).
  -f [geojson|geojsonseq|geoparquet]
                                  [default: geojsonseq]
  -o, --output PATH
  -r, --release TEXT
  --help                          Show this message and exit.

